; str-find-cost-run.fk — re-derive what one str_find over a large string costs,
; instead of trusting the numbers somebody wrote down once.
;
; HOW TO ASK IT. The cell reads whatever is at the target path and searches it
; once for a token that is not in it, so the search runs to the end and cannot
; stop early on a lucky hit:
;
;   head -c 3866624 cognition/concept-text-senses-10000.tsv > /tmp/str-find-cost-target
;   /usr/bin/time -p ./fkwu observe/str-find-cost-run.fk
;
; Vary the byte count and watch whether seconds-per-megabyte stays flat. That
; ratio, not the absolute time, is the reading: a search that costs more per
; megabyte as the string grows is not merely slow, it is degrading, and the
; degradation is a different defect from the constant.
;
; THE TARGET PATH IS SHARED GROUND — a sibling running this at the same moment
; writes the same file, and you would time THEIR bytes and call the number
; yours. Change the one line below if another lane is live.
;
; WHAT IT MEASURED, 2026-08-25, Apple M4 Max, one run each, cold .fkb removed:
;
;                     allocating loop     byte-wise loop
;     1.0 MB              3.30 s              0.21 s
;     2.0 MB              8.04 s              0.24 s
;     3.7 MB             21.92 s              0.50 s
;
; Per megabyte the old form went 3.3 -> 3.9 -> 5.9 seconds, so it got worse the
; longer the string; the new one stays near a tenth of a second. The speedup
; therefore is not one number — it is 16x at a megabyte and 44x at 3.7 MB, and
; it keeps growing, because what was removed was the degradation and not just
; the constant.
;
; These readings are one run each on a host that has been observed to vary 19%
; between two runs of identical work. A 16x difference survives that spread by
; two orders of magnitude; a 20% difference measured here would not, and should
; not be reported from a single run.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk

(do
    (defn sfc-target-file () "/tmp/str-find-cost-target")
    (defn sfc-absent-token () "ZZZZ-not-in-any-real-text-ZZZZ")

    (defn sfc-line (name value)
        (print_str (str_concat name (str_concat value "\n"))))

    (defn sfc-run ()
        (if (eq (fs_exists (sfc-target-file)) 0)
            (do (sfc-line "str-find-cost-run: write the bytes to " (sfc-target-file))
                -1)
            (do
                (let s (read_file (sfc-target-file)))
                (sfc-line "bytes " (int_to_str (str_len s)))
                ; the whole measurement is this one call; time the process
                (let at (str_find s (sfc-absent-token) 0))
                (sfc-line "found " (int_to_str at))
                (if (eq at -1) 0 1))))

    (sfc-run))
